1
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,610
Ah, Sinon!

2
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:00,300
You're late, Kitty. Kirito.

3
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,290
Who's there?

4
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:05,600
I've been out here so long.

5
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:06,940
I might catch cold.

6
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:10,590
Sugo!

7
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:12,980
You did a very bad thing, Kirito.

8
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:15,840
You know, I can still feel the pain.

9
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:17,340
It's over, Sugo.

10
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:19,460
You better turn yourself in.

11
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,860
You're finished.

12
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:23,310
Finished?

13
00:01:23,393 --> 00:01:24,223
Hardly.

14
00:01:24,306 --> 00:01:27,778
There are lots of companies that
would kill to have me in my research.

15
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:33,097
And once it's complete there won't be
anything or anyone standing in my way,

16
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:35,377
then I'll be the god of this world.

17
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:38,640
Oh But first first I'm going to kill you.

18
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:48,800
Come on get up I said get up!

19
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:58,177
You think a piece of trash
like you can get in my way?

20
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,620
Did you think I'd let you slow me down?

21
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,760
Wanna know what the punishment is?

22
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:04,930
Death.

23
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:08,020
I won't accept anything less.

24
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:15,850
Damn.

25
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,797
My right eye's all foggy.

26
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,060
But I won't miss again, promise.

27
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,180
You bastard!

28
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:30,200
You little boy.

29
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:32,260
You're a piece of scum!

30
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:34,185
You don't have any real power!

31
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:39,380
And neither do you, Sugo.

32
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:43,000
I damn you!

33
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:48,730
No!

34
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:55,400
Such a weak weapon.

35
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:56,840
Too light.

36
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:58,340
No reach.

37
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:02,880
And it's all I'm gonna need
to kill you once and for all.

38
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:44,580
Oh, my God.

39
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,282
Hurry up, she's waiting for you.

40
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:40,620
Asuna.

41
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:45,240
Kirito. Asuna.

42
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,157
It's okay now.

43
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,077
It's over.

44
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:05,040
I fought the final boss just
now and the last battle's over.

45
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:07,360
It's all over.

46
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:14,157
I'm sorry but I can't
hear too well right now.

47
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:17,320
I think I know what you said though.

48
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:21,460
What you meant that it's really over?

49
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:27,220
And finally, finally, I get to meet you.

50
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:36,040
So anyway, I'm Asuna, Asuna Yuki.

51
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:38,360
And I'm finally back.

52
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,940
I'm Kazuto Kirigaya.

53
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,520
Welcome home, Asuna.

54
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,630
Thank you.

55
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:26,348
I can't wait to see the
feeling of the pain.

56
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:32,360
It's a true promise.

57
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,401
I'm telling you.

58
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:49,677
I'm not sure what I'm doing.

59
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,597
I'll just say that I'm not going to die.

60
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:52,510
I'm not going to die.

61
00:06:52,593 --> 00:06:55,517
I'm not going to die.

62
00:06:55,600 --> 00:07:01,477
I'm not going to die.

63
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:03,400
Oh.

64
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:03,100
Looking at this sentence,
Could anyone tell me how...

65
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,842
Looks like that's all for today.

66
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:09,080
Keep an eye out for
Homework Files 25 and 26.

67
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:12,321
And make sure to upload
your answers by next week.

68
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:15,213
Hey, can I come to you?

69
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,269
Thanks for waiting for me.

70
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,477
I'm tired.

71
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,660
Tired and hungry.

72
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:42,957
You're starting to sound
like an old man, Kirito.

73
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:47,569
Yeah, well, I feel like I've gotten
about five years older in the last month.

74
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:51,460
And by the way, it's
not Kirito, it's Kazuto.

75
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:52,940
This is real life.

76
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,497
You shouldn't call someone
by their avatar's name here.

77
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:57,020
Oh, sorry! I forgot!

78
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:59,260
Oh no, now what am I gonna do?

79
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:00,557
Everyone will know it's me!

80
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:04,228
That's what you get for using
your real name for your avatar.

81
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,290
Eh,

82
00:09:05,373 --> 00:09:08,797
I guess it doesn't really matter because
everyone at our school is stuck in SAO,

83
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:09,710
same as us.

84
00:09:09,793 --> 00:09:11,524
My cover's probably blown, too.

85
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:17,439
Asuna, are you getting around okay?

86
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,231
I mean, is the rehab you're doing helping?

87
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:23,877
I finally got the okay to walk
around without my crutches.

88
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:27,660
Although, the doctors say I
shouldn't run just yet. You will.

89
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:31,440
By the way, Kirito... What?

90
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:36,140
Do you know that everyone
in the cafeteria can see us?

91
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:45,289
Seriously, that little oversight
is going to cost you lunch.

92
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:46,800
Sorry, I didn't know.

93
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:51,980
Daddy!

94
00:09:57,900 --> 00:09:59,724
I was wondering about your dad.

95
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:01,020
Is he okay? Mm-hmm.

96
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:04,117
He is, but he's still not
over this whole thing.

97
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:06,788
He quit as CEO and took
an early retirement.

98
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:10,777
And now that he's got all this free
time, he doesn't know what to do with it.

99
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:14,337
Hopefully dad can find a hobby
and maybe that'll cheer him up.

100
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:15,400
I hope so.

101
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:22,044
That night in the parking lot,
the police came and arrested Sugo.

102
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:27,837
Later when they interrogated him he denied

103
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:30,177
everything and tried to
pin the blame on Akihiko

104
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:33,217
Kayaba but after the police questioned one

105
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:36,360
of his employees Sugo
confessed to everything

106
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:41,557
As for those 300 SAO players
when they came to they

107
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:44,737
couldn't remember anything
about the experiments The good

108
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:47,457
thing is they didn't suffer
any neurological or psychiatric

109
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:50,760
after effects so everyone
can go back to their lives.

110
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:54,180
But the fate of virtual
Miss was a different story.

111
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:58,481
This latest incident practically
destroyed the industry altogether.

112
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:03,380
In the end, wrecked
progress was dismantled.

113
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:06,480
Its parent company also
suffered a big hit.

114
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,060
ALO was shut down.

115
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:10,640
No surprise there.

116
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:13,900
And as for the five or six other VR Miss,

117
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:17,021
with all the negative press
and the public outcry,

118
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:18,985
Their days were numbered, too.

119
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:22,677
You know who I was just thinking about?

120
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:23,590
The commander.

121
00:11:23,740 --> 00:11:24,757
What happened to him?

122
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:25,680
Hmm? Oh.

123
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:27,590
Yeah.

124
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,190
Kayaba's dead.

125
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,960
They say it was suicide.

126
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,120
No way. Yeah,

127
00:11:33,340 --> 00:11:34,917
when the world of SAO collapsed,

128
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,477
he did a high-output scan on his
brain and fried it when it was over.

129
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:39,390
So, wait.

130
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:42,737
Was he trying to copy his
consciousness to the net or something?

131
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:47,408
Well, it's one in a thousand shot for
it to work, but I know he pulled it off.

132
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,940
That day, Kayaba spoke to me.

133
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,160
Or his consciousness did anyway.

134
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:55,690
What's this?

135
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,565
The beginnings of a new world.

136
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,040
I call it the seed.

137
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:03,220
Once it sprouts, you'll know what it is.

138
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:05,601
What you do with it is up to you.

139
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,939
You can even delete it if you want.

140
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:09,350
However,

141
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:12,937
if you still have a tiny bit of
fondness left for the virtual world,

142
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:14,373
you'll take care of it.

143
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:18,060
Kirito? Kirito?

144
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:20,777
Don't forget, we're
meeting the others later.

145
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:21,690
Huh?

146
00:12:21,773 --> 00:12:22,603
Oh, yeah, right.

147
00:12:22,686 --> 00:12:23,617
Sorry, I was spacing out.

148
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:24,540
As always.

149
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:27,697
It doesn't matter whether
you're in the game or IRL.

150
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:30,662
The minute you relax, you
space out like a champ.

151
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:44,245
Seriously, Rika, you're driving
me crazy with all that slurping.

152
00:12:44,780 --> 00:12:46,197
Leave me alone.

153
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:48,840
He's all over her and
it's driving me nuts.

154
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:52,280
Acting like that at school, it's so tacky.

155
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:55,869
Spying on them's kinda
tacky too, you know.

156
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,897
If I'd have known it
was gonna be like this,

157
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:02,497
I wouldn't have let you talk
me into a Montbonk truce.

158
00:13:02,580 --> 00:13:04,977
I didn't talk you into
it, it was your idea!

159
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:08,517
You said we should let them have their
little romance for a month, remember?

160
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:10,500
I mean, God, talk about naive.

161
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:18,835
It's going to be cool meeting
everyone today, isn't it?

162
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:22,100
Yeah, I can't wait!

163
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,620
Sugu, I forgot to ask before.

164
00:13:35,860 --> 00:13:36,877
Did you ever meet Egill?

165
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:40,254
Yeah, we went hunting together
a couple of times in ALO.

166
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:41,957
His avatar's ginormous!

167
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:45,277
Yeah, well get ready because
he's that big in real life too.

168
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:47,242
Prepare to have your mind blown.

169
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:00,080
Hold on a sec.

170
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:02,436
Were we supposed to get here earlier?

171
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:06,777
We gave you a later time to make
sure everyone else got here first.

172
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:09,697
It wouldn't be right for the guests of
honor to show up before all the guests.

173
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:12,540
Don't just stand there,
come on in. Uh, hey.

174
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:15,197
Okay, let's get this party started.

175
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:16,692
You all know what to do.

176
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,277
Ready, and...

177
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:21,720
Congratulations on beating SAO, Kittito!

178
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:27,910
Cheers!

179
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:29,190
Cheers!

180
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:39,102
Bartender, bourbon on the rocks.

181
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:45,910
Whoa, dude.

182
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,157
This is Long tea.

183
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,070
Thank you.

184
00:14:48,153 --> 00:14:49,311
Slide me a big boy drink.

185
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,120
Klein, seriously?

186
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:53,954
Aren't you supposed to go back to work?

187
00:14:55,860 --> 00:14:58,300
Alcohol makes the overtime go by faster.

188
00:14:59,080 --> 00:14:59,910
Uh-oh.

189
00:14:59,993 --> 00:15:00,823
Chick alert.

190
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,760
Long time no see. Hi, thinker.

191
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,237
How have you been?

192
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:08,577
I heard that you and
Yulia are married now.

193
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:11,400
I know it's late, but congrats.

194
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:13,290
Thank you.

195
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:14,717
But ever since we got back,

196
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:17,657
it's been taking everything
we've got to adjust to life here.

197
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:20,537
The good thing is, I'm
settling into work mode again.

198
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,737
Congratulations on getting that far.

199
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:25,900
Hey, I've been reading the
new MMO today. Nice job.

200
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:27,737
Yeah, I wish it were better.

201
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:30,055
It could have used a bit more content.

202
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:34,480
Oh, well, with the way Miss are now,
who needs walkthroughs and news?

203
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:36,817
Those things are going to
be irrelevant soon anyway.

204
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:39,597
You know what they say about
how the universe was born.

205
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,974
First there was chaos.

206
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:44,420
By the way, Egil, has
the seed been doing okay?

207
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:46,220
It's doing amazing.

208
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:49,040
We got 50 mirrors already set up.

209
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:51,660
It's been downloaded 100,000 times.

210
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:53,037
And check this out.

211
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:56,002
It's got 300 big-ass
servers actually running it.

212
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,360
After I visited Asuna at the hospital,

213
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:02,837
I took the thing Kayaba
called the seed over to Egil?

214
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,685
and asked him to check it out.

215
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:09,337
Turned out it was a full-dive
MMO that Kayaba developed.

216
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:12,420
It came in a program package
called the World Seed,

217
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:17,167
a stripped-down version of the Cardinal
system that could run on small servers.

218
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:21,577
Kayaba had modified the program so
that anyone with access to an ordinary

219
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:26,425
server could easily download it and use
it to create their very own online world.

220
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:29,640
After Egil said it was safe to use,

221
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:31,677
I had him upload it to servers across the

222
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:34,584
globe so that everyone
could access it for free.

223
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:41,520
It turned out that was exactly what virtual
Miss needed to keep the genre going.

224
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:46,557
As for Alfheim Online, all the data
was transferred to a new company?

225
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:49,169
that decided to keep
it online and running.

226
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:53,226
But the new Alfheim wasn't the
only world born out of the seed.

227
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:57,237
Everyone from individual
gamers to a few hundred small

228
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:59,757
companies were suddenly
creating brand new worlds?

229
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:02,134
on their very own virtual game servers.

230
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:05,777
The best part is they were
all connected to each other.

231
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:09,177
It's almost to the point where you
could create a character in one world,

232
00:17:09,260 --> 00:17:12,495
then transfer it to another
with all its skills intact.

233
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:18,659
Hey, has anything changed
for tonight's after party?

234
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:20,527
Nope, we're still on for 11.

235
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,099
We're meeting up in Yggdrasil City.

236
00:17:40,980 --> 00:17:43,800
I don't know.

237
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:23,769
You know, I had a feeling you
were going to fly too high up.

238
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:26,256
It's almost 11, so I came to get you.

239
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:28,840
Oh, okay, thanks.

240
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:34,360
Hey, Kazut, er, Kirito,

241
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:38,240
you know how ALO's got a
new company running it now,

242
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:41,479
and how you can use your
old SAO avatar if you want?

243
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:45,760
Everyone else is using their old
avatar, so how come you're not?

244
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,230
Hmm.

245
00:18:49,313 --> 00:18:52,684
I guess because in that world,
that Kirito's mission is over now.

246
00:18:54,580 --> 00:18:55,620
I guess so.

247
00:18:57,620 --> 00:19:00,257
Then I was the first to
meet the Spriggan version

248
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:03,222
of Kirito and show him
the way to the world tree.

249
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:04,940
That's pretty cool.

250
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:09,220
Hey, Kirito!

251
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:12,040
Dance with me. Huh? Dance!

252
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:14,597
It's an advanced
technique I just mastered.

253
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:17,820
You just hover, then
slowly spin on your X-axis.

254
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:21,850
That's it!

255
00:19:21,933 --> 00:19:23,391
Yeah, you're doing great!

